          <title>Hospital Course</title>
          <text><paragraph>Mrs. Whitfield, a 68-year-old woman, was admitted with three days of worsening shortness of breath and leg swelling. She was treated with intravenous diuretics and lost 4.2 kg of fluid. Echocardiography showed an ejection fraction of 35%. Kidney function was monitored closely and stayed near her baseline.</paragraph><paragraph>She was discharged home in stable condition. Follow-up with Dr. Achterberg in one week; call (555) 010-3300 with weight gain above 1.5 kg in two days.</paragraph></text>
        </section>
